-- title:
--   Normal Noetherian local domain of dimension one is regular
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain, Noetherian, local, and integrally closed in its field of fractions, and suppose that its Krull dimension, taken in the extended sense as an element of $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\pm\infty\}$ via `ringKrullDim`, is equal to $1$. Then $R$ is a regular local ring in the sense of Mathlib's `IsRegularLocalRing`: the maximal ideal of $R$ is generated by a set of cardinality equal to the Krull dimension of $R$, equivalently the embedding dimension $\dim_{\kappa}\mathfrak{m}/\mathfrak{m}^2$ agrees with $\dim R$. The conclusion is delivered as a statement about $R$ itself, not about any completion or localisation.
--
--   This is the standard characterisation of discrete valuation rings among one-dimensional normal Noetherian local domains, recast as a regularity statement; in dimension one regularity is exactly the condition that the maximal ideal be principal. It is used to verify regularity of the localisations of a normal one-dimensional ring at its primes, which is how [`IsIntegrallyClosed.isRegularLocalRing_localization_atPrime_of_ringKrullDim_eq_one`](thm.html#IsIntegrallyClosed.isRegularLocalRing_localization_atPrime_of_ringKrullDim_eq_one) consumes it.
